The idea is to make items slightly more fun, and a tad bit more
difficult to identify.

Wand of Harm Self
-does not ask for a direction: is always targeted towards yourself.
-when broken, the magical explosion deals d20, only towards yourself.
-engraving with the wand causes it to zap.
-is never generated blessed.
blessed
Confuses or stuns you.
("Your mind spins wildly!")
uncursed
Adds the effects of hallucination ("Far out, dude!"), wands of
striking, magic missile, fire, cold, and lightning to the list of
possible effects. Additionally, abuses your stats.

cursed
Adds the effects of polymorph, bad sex, bad spellbooks, and cursed
potions to the list of possible effects. Additionally, has the effect
of a cursed potion of gain ability.

Wand of Darkness
-when engraving, zaps the wand.
blessed
The area around you is darkened.
uncursed
You are blinded.
cursed
You are blinded, and suffer from malignant aura.

Wand of Undeath
-no message when engraving
-when broken, acts as a wand of undead turning
-beams and touches of death will cause the wand to explode
You are polymorphed into the appropriate type of zombie. If you are
currently a living creature without an appropriate type of zombie, you
are reverted to your original form and then zombified. If you are
already undead, no effect.

Wand of Destroy Armor
-zaps at self when engraving
-when broken, deals n15 damage to non-magic resistant creatures in
vicinity; destroys armor
Fires a beam of destroy armor; destroys a random piece of armor.
If cursed, has a chance of firing at yourself.

Ring of Sliming
-begins the sliming process.
-if sliming is stopped, ring is destroyed.
-auto-identifies.

Ring of Paralysis
-you are frozen to the ground for n300 turns.
-the ring dissolves after the effect takes place.
-auto-identifies.

Ring of Magic Portal
-you are branch-ported; randomly if not blessed.
-ring is used up when used up.

Anti-Personnel Ring
-you suffer from an exploded land mine.
-ring is used up when used up.

Amulet of Entering Explore Mode
-You enter explore mode.
("You put on the amulet of entering explore mode... you feel your score
draining away!")
-I'm just kidding. Sorry.

Amulet of Anchoring
-acts like a loadstone if cursed
-otherwise, prevents you from teleporting

Amulet versus Oxidation
-your items will not rust further
-you gain rust resistance

Amulet versus Water
-drys up moats, pools of water, rust traps, and fountains adjacent to
you
-has a chance of being used up each time this occurs
-clerics will not attack you with geysers

Amulet versus Fire
-your items will not burn further
-you gain fire resistance

Amulet versus Earth
-you take d2 damage every time you step on solid ground
-provides water walking
-this is considered a major problem

Amulet versus Air
-see; amulet of strangulation; amulet of magical breathing



